# Commands

- debug / release presets: default `zpc` builds (macOS, Linux, and docker)
- `cmake --workflow --preset <preset>`: Configure and build the project for the given preset.
- `cmake --preset <preset>`: Configure the project and regenerate the command classes.
- `cmake --build --preset <preset>`: Build the project for the given preset.

- unit-test preset: `unit-test` (macOS, Linux, and docker; ASan, UBSan, LSan on Linux via `ASAN_OPTIONS`; halt on sanitizer error)
- `cmake --workflow --preset unit-test --fresh`: Configure, build, and run unit tests. `--fresh` removes the existing CMake cache in `build/unit-test`.
- `cmake --preset unit-test --fresh`: Configure the project with unit tests enabled.
- `cmake --build --preset unit-test`: Build the unit-test targets.
- `ctest --preset unit-test`: Run unit tests after they have been built.
- debug-sanitize preset: Debug `zpc` with ASan and UBSan. Linux: `cpack --preset debug-sanitize` → `build/debug-sanitize/zpc-<arch>-debug-sanitize.deb`. Scheduled sanitizer CI; not a release artifact.
- debug-tsan preset: Debug `zpc` with TSan only. Linux: `cpack --preset debug-tsan` → `build/debug-tsan/zpc-<arch>-debug-tsan.deb`. Same sanitizer CI; not a release artifact.
- Linux packaging (CI): after `cmake --workflow --preset release` with `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`, run `cpack --preset release`. Output: `build/release/*.deb`.
- PR CI build jobs: macOS and Linux amd64-gcc build `debug` then `release`; arm64-gcc and Linux clang build `release` only. Package gcc `release` only.
